Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AESinkALSA: opt Auge HDMI HD passthrough into IEC pause carrier

Plug CoreELEC's Amlogic ALSA path into Kodi's generic optional pause-carrier
policy. Enable it by default only for opened Auge HDMI TrueHD and DTS-HD
passthrough streams. PCM, S/PDIF, USB and other devices retain their policy.

The setting does not extend keepalive, certify receiver readiness or suppress
synchronization. It avoids selecting zero filler solely because STREAMING is
false while an eligible transport remains open. Software pause, buffering and
same-format seeks all share that existing idle-carrier path.

This is a bounded carrier-policy experiment for late sound after unpause.
Do not use snd_pcm_pause: AML's pause release can reset the FIFO and mute the
receiver. Keep this platform opt-in separate from the generic cache and sink
changes; no addon or runtime plugin installation is needed.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.h b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.h
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.h
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@
   double GetCacheTotal() override;
   unsigned int AddPackets(uint8_t **data, unsigned int frames, unsigned int offset) override;
   void Drain() override;
+  bool WantsIECPauseBursts() const override;
 
 private:
   CAEChannelInfo GetChannelLayoutRaw(const AEAudioFormat& format);
@@ -112,4 +113,3 @@
 
   static void sndLibErrorHandler(const char *file, int line, const char *function, int err, const char *fmt, ...);
 };
-
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
@@ -743,6 +743,19 @@
   }
 }
 
+bool CAESinkALSA::WantsIECPauseBursts() const
+{
+  // CoreELEC's AML HDMI integration opts into Kodi's generic idle-carrier
+  // policy. Limit the initial change to the Auge HD passthrough paths; PCM,
+  // USB, S/PDIF and unrelated ALSA devices retain the generic default.
+  const auto type = m_initFormat.m_streamInfo.m_type;
+  return m_pcm && m_passthrough && GetAMLDeviceType(m_device) == AML_AUGESOUND &&
+         AEDeviceTypeFromName(m_device) == AE_DEVTYPE_HDMI &&
+         (type == CAEStreamInfo::STREAM_TYPE_TRUEHD ||
+          type == CAEStreamInfo::STREAM_TYPE_DTSHD ||
+          type == CAEStreamInfo::STREAM_TYPE_DTSHD_MA);
+}
+
 bool CAESinkALSA::Initialize(AEAudioFormat &format, std::string &device)
 {
   m_initDevice = device;
